    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0053" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v20/pg25"/>

                <head>12. Letter From President Nasser to President Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d12-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Cairo</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1967-12-09"
                            >December 9, 1967</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Dear Mr. President:</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity to extend my best wishes to you and your family.</p>
                <p>At this time which is sacred to both our people I feel that good relations should
                    exist between our people.</p>
                <p>I have sent a special message through Mr. Birdsall. I trust
                    you will receive it in the spirit which I send it.</p>
                <p>With highest personal regards.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Jamal Abdul Nasser</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d12-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d12-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, United Arab
                    Republic, Vol. VI, Memos, 8/67–7/68. No classification marking. The letter was
                    delivered to President Johnson by
                        James Birdsall on December 18; see <ref target="#d21"
                        >Document 21</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
